#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/rest-api/cti.md:258 src/en/reference/rest-api/cti.md:374
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`direction` <Badge type=\"info\" text=\"in\" />:\n"
": The call direction - if your agent initiates a call, this will be `out`.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/rest-api/cti.md:262 src/en/reference/rest-api/cti.md:378
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`callId` <Badge type=\"info\" text=\"53ba82e2bd6d12d9fb2d3838f0cfb070\" />:\n"
": An ID that is unique for the call. Zammad will use this ID to identify an\n"
"  existing call with following actions (e.g. like answering or hanging up).\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/rest-api/cti.md:270 src/en/reference/rest-api/cti.md:398
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`answeringNumber` <Badge type=\"info\" text=\"493055571600\" />:\n"
": Zammad will look up for a user with given value, the following attributes\n"
"  will be evaluated in given order:\n"
"  - `user.phone`\n"
"  - `user.login`\n"
"  - `user.if`\n"
"  This value is optional.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/rest-api/cti.md:276
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`user` <Badge type=\"info\" text=\"John Doe\" />:\n"
": The user(s) real name involved. You may have to provide array style (`[]`)\n"
"  params depending on the call method you choose. If the direction is `out`,\n"
"  this is the name of the calling person(s). If the direction is `in`, this is\n"
"  the name of the called person(s). This value is optional.\n"
msgstr ""

