#. type: Title ##
#: src/en/reference/rest-api/intro.md:31
#, no-wrap
msgid "Authentication"
msgstr "Аутентификација"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/rest-api/intro.md:34
msgid "Zammad supports three different authentication methods for its API."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: src/en/reference/rest-api/intro.md:35
#, no-wrap
msgid "HTTP Basic Authentication (username/password)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/rest-api/intro.md:41
msgid ""
"The username / password must be provided as HTTP header in the HTTP call.  "
"This authentication method can be disabled and may not be available in your "
"system."
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (sh)
#: src/en/reference/rest-api/intro.md:42
#, no-wrap
msgid "$ curl -u {username}:{password} https://{fqdn}/{endpoint}\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced div block (warning)
#: src/en/reference/rest-api/intro.md:46
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We strongly suggest against using basic authentication. Use access\n"
"tokens when ever possible!\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: src/en/reference/rest-api/intro.md:51
#, no-wrap
msgid "HTTP Token Authentication (access token)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/rest-api/intro.md:57
msgid ""
"The access token must be provided as HTTP header in the HTTP call.  Each "
"user can create several access tokens in their user preferences.  This "
"authentication method can be disabled and may not be available in your "
"system."
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (sh)
#: src/en/reference/rest-api/intro.md:58
#, no-wrap
msgid "$ curl -H \"Authorization: Token token={your_token}\" https://{fqdn}/{endpoint}\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: src/en/reference/rest-api/intro.md:62
#, no-wrap
msgid "OAuth2 (token access)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/rest-api/intro.md:65
msgid ""
"The token must be provided as HTTP header in your calls.  This allows 3rd "
"party applications to authenticate against Zammad."
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced code block (sh)
#: src/en/reference/rest-api/intro.md:66
#, no-wrap
msgid "$ curl -H \"Authorization: Bearer {your_token}\" https://{fqdn}/{endpoint}\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: src/en/reference/rest-api/intro.md:70
#, no-wrap
msgid "Endpoints and Example Data"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/reference/rest-api/intro.md:77
msgid ""
"For simplicity we'll not provide specific commands on the next pages, but "
"instead tell the possible call method (e.g. `GET`) and the endpoint to use "
"(e.g. `/api/v1/users`). In case Zammad expects information within these "
"endpoint urls, we'll put them into curly braces like so: `/api/v1/users/"
"{user id}`"
