#. type: Title #
#: src/en/tutorials/backup-restore.md:1 src/en/tutorials/backup-restore.md:6
#, no-wrap
msgid "Backup & Restore"
msgstr "Резервна копија и њено враћање"

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/tutorials/backup-restore.md:9
msgid ""
"Zammad ships scripts in package installations for backup & restore which you "
"can use."
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced div block (warning)
#: src/en/tutorials/backup-restore.md:10
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"These scripts do not come with any warranty and may not work in your specific\n"
"use case. This depends on the configuration and installation type of your\n"
"instance.\n"
"\n"
"You should always regularly test and review the functionality! If the script\n"
"functionality or scope is not working for your cases, feel free to copy these\n"
"to a independent location and adjust the scripts as needed.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/tutorials/backup-restore.md:21
msgid "There are some limitations you should know:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/tutorials/backup-restore.md:32
msgid "These scripts won't work in container based installations."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/tutorials/backup-restore.md:32
msgid "They only work for PostgreSQL installations."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/tutorials/backup-restore.md:32
msgid "The backup is always a full dump (no incremental backup)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/tutorials/backup-restore.md:32
msgid ""
"Partial backup and restore (e.g. only specific data like tickets,users) is "
"not possible."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/tutorials/backup-restore.md:32
msgid "Switching database system is not possible."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/tutorials/backup-restore.md:32
msgid "System settings (like environment variables) are not backed up."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/tutorials/backup-restore.md:32
msgid "Restore to an older Zammad version is not possible."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/tutorials/backup-restore.md:32
msgid ""
"Do not restore backup files from custom scripts with the provided scripts by "
"Zammad. This might cause problems."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/tutorials/backup-restore.md:37
msgid ""
"The scripts are located in `/opt/zammad/contrib/backup`. The following files "
"are relevant:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/tutorials/backup-restore.md:41
msgid "Backup configuration file: `config.dist`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/tutorials/backup-restore.md:41
msgid "Script for backing up your data: `zammad_backup.sh`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/tutorials/backup-restore.md:41
msgid "Script for restoring your data: `zammad_restore.sh`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/tutorials/backup-restore.md:43
msgid ""
"To execute a backup based on the default configuration, follow the steps "
"below:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '1. '
#: src/en/tutorials/backup-restore.md:50
msgid "Copy the `config.dist` file to `config`."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '1. '
#: src/en/tutorials/backup-restore.md:50
msgid ""
"Change default parameters in the config file if needed. See [Backup "
"Configuration](#backup-config-parametersbackup-config-parameters) for "
"details."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '1. '
#: src/en/tutorials/backup-restore.md:50
#, fuzzy
#| msgid "Get started with Zammad"
msgid "Stop Zammad `systemctl stop zammad`"
msgstr "Први кораци са Zammad-ом"

#. type: Bullet: '1. '
#: src/en/tutorials/backup-restore.md:50
msgid ""
"Execute `/opt/zammad/contrib/backup/zammad_backup.sh` (as `root` or `zammad` "
"user)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: src/en/tutorials/backup-restore.md:51
#, no-wrap
msgid "Backup Configuration"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/tutorials/backup-restore.md:55
msgid ""
"You can find details about the configuration parameters with default values "
"below."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/tutorials/backup-restore.md:60
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`BACKUP_DIR` <Badge type=\"info\" text=\"/var/tmp/zammad_backup\"/>\n"
": Location where the script writes the backup files to. The directory will be\n"
"  created if it does not exist. Make sure you have enough space because the\n"
"  script writes full dumps.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/tutorials/backup-restore.md:65
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`HOLD_DAYS` <Badge type=\"info\" text=\"10\"/>\n"
": Define how many days the backup script should keep old backups. This value\n"
"  contains a 60 minutes grace period (e.g. 10 days plus 1 hour) for safety\n"
"  reasons. Old backups are removed before creating the a new backup.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/tutorials/backup-restore.md:69
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"  Examples:\n"
"  - `1` will keep backups of the last 25 hours\n"
"  - `-1` will remove all available backups (except the new one)\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/tutorials/backup-restore.md:73
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`FULL_FS_DUMP` <Badge type=\"info\" text=\"yes\"/>\n"
": - `yes`: the backup includes also application files.\n"
"  - `no`: the backup includes only user data.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/tutorials/backup-restore.md:76
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"  In any case, it includes the Zammad database and the attachments, if you\n"
"  stored them in the file system. If you are in doubt, set this to no.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/tutorials/backup-restore.md:79
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"``DEBUG`` <Badge type=\"info\" text=\"no\"/>\n"
": Setting this option to `yes` will output useful debug messages.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced div block (warning)
#: src/en/tutorials/backup-restore.md:79
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"  This option potentially returns sensitive information to standard output! Do\n"
"  not use this option in production environments or ensure to turn it off after\n"
"  testing.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: src/en/tutorials/backup-restore.md:85
#, no-wrap
msgid "Restore Backups"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: src/en/tutorials/backup-restore.md:87
#, no-wrap
msgid "Important Information"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/tutorials/backup-restore.md:90
msgid ""
"Please read the following information carefully before starting to restore "
"your data."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/tutorials/backup-restore.md:101
msgid ""
"This section is **not** about **migrating from one host to another**. You "
"can find instructions about this topic in the [next section](#migrate-to-a-"
"new-host)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/tutorials/backup-restore.md:101
msgid "This guide expects a fully installed Zammad version"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/tutorials/backup-restore.md:101
msgid ""
"It also expects you to restore Zammad on the same host and Zammad version"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/tutorials/backup-restore.md:101
msgid ""
"The restore process stops & restarts Zammad. Therefore you have to run the "
"restore script with appropriate permissions (e.g. as root)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/tutorials/backup-restore.md:101
msgid "PostgreSQL based installations will drop and re-create the database!"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/tutorials/backup-restore.md:101
msgid ""
"At least twice the backed up Zammad instance size of free storage is "
"required. If you have the dump only, factor 3 could be a good number."
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced div block (tip)
#: src/en/tutorials/backup-restore.md:102
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"If your scenario is different as described above, please consult the\n"
"[Zammad Community](https://community.zammad.org/c/trouble-running-zammad-this-is-your-place/5) or consider\n"
