#. type: Fenced div block (tip)
#: src/en/tutorials/migrate.md:405
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In some cases restarting your webserver may help to solve internal server\n"
"errors.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced div block (tabs)
#: src/en/tutorials/migrate.md:413
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"\n"
"=== Via Browser\n"
"\n"
"After installing Zammad and\n"
"[configuring your webserver](/en/tutorials/webserver-config), navigate to your\n"
"Zammads FQDN in your browser and follow the migration wizard. You can find\n"
"it in the log in screen by clicking the \"Or migrate from another system\"\n"
"link at the bottom.\n"
"\n"
"Depending on the size of your OTRS installation this may take a while. In such\n"
"a case, consider using the command line version of this feature. This also\n"
"applies if you experience timeouts during the migration.\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"=== Via Console\n"
"\n"
"Open console:\n"
"\n"
"```bash\n"
"zammad run rails c\n"
"```\n"
"Set variables (ensure to replace *xxx* with your values):\n"
"\n"
"```bash\n"
"Setting.set('import_otrs_endpoint', 'https://xxx/otrs/public.pl?Action=ZammadMigrator')\n"
"```\n"
"```bash\n"
"Setting.set('import_otrs_endpoint_key', 'xxx')\n"
"```\n"
"```bash\n"
"Setting.set('import_mode', true)\n"
"```\n"
"\n"
"Run a full migration:\n"
"\n"
"```bash\n"
"Import::OTRS.start\n"
"```\n"
"\n"
"Run a differential migration (only possible after finishing an earlier full\n"
"migration):\n"
"\n"
"All steps from \"Set variables\" +\n"
"\n"
"```bash\n"
"Setting.set('system_init_done', false)\n"
"```\n"
"\n"
"```bash\n"
"Import::OTRS.diff_worker\n"
"```\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: src/en/tutorials/migrate.md:482
#, no-wrap
msgid "Zendesk"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/tutorials/migrate.md:498
msgid ""
"Important: Please note that migration speed highly depends on your Zendesk "
"plan (API rate limits apply)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/tutorials/migrate.md:498
msgid ""
"Your Zendesk plan has to provide API support. This may not apply to all "
"available plans."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/tutorials/migrate.md:498
msgid ""
"User passwords are not migrated and will require the user to use the "
"password reset link on the login page."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/tutorials/migrate.md:498
msgid ""
"Objects with cyrillic strings can't be migrated. Make sure to rename them "
"before starting the migration."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/tutorials/migrate.md:506
msgid ""
"Zammad requires API access which is why you’ll need to [create an API key]"
"(https://support.zendesk.com/hc/en-us/articles/4408889192858-Generating-a-"
"new-API-token)  for the migration. The migrator will request your Zendesk-"
"URL, email address and API key."
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced div block (tabs)
#: src/en/tutorials/migrate.md:518
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"\n"
"=== Via Browser\n"
"\n"
"After installing Zammad and\n"
"[configuring your webserver](/en/tutorials/webserver-config), navigate to your\n"
"Zammads FQDN in your browser and follow the migration wizard. You can find\n"
"it in the log in screen by clicking the \"Or migrate from another system\"\n"
"link at the bottom.\n"
"\n"
"Depending on the the number of users, tickets and Zendesk plan, this may take a\n"
"while.\n"
"\n"
"=== Via Console\n"
"\n"
"Open console:\n"
"\n"
"```bash\n"
"zammad run rails c\n"
"```\n"
"Set variables:\n"
"\n"
"```bash\n"
"subdomain = '{zendesk url}'\n"
"```\n"
"```bash\n"
"email = '{zendesk admin email address}'\n"
"```\n"
"```bash\n"
"token = '{zendesk token}'\n"
"\n"
"```\n"
"\n"
"Update Zammad settings:\n"
"```bash\n"
"Setting.set('import_zendesk_endpoint', \"https://#{subdomain}/api/v2\")\n"
"```\n"
"```bash\n"
"Setting.set('import_zendesk_endpoint_username', email)\n"
"```\n"
"```bash\n"
"Setting.set('import_zendesk_endpoint_key', token)\n"
"```\n"
"```bash\n"
"Setting.set('import_backend', 'zendesk')\n"
"```\n"
"```bash\n"
"Setting.set('import_mode', true)\n"
"```\n"
"Check your configuration in a dry run:\n"
"\n"
"```bash\n"
"Sequencer.process('Import::Zendesk::ConnectionTest')\n"
"```\n"
"\n"
"Run the migration:\n"
"\n"
"```bash\n"
"job = ImportJob.create(name: 'Import::Zendesk')\n"
"```\n"
"```bash\n"
"AsyncImportJob.perform_later(job)\n"
"```\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title #
#: src/en/tutorials/webserver-config.md:1
#: src/en/tutorials/webserver-config.md:6
#, no-wrap
msgid "Webserver Configuration"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/tutorials/webserver-config.md:14
msgid ""
"This guide is only relevant for package installations. During the "
"installation, Zammad tries to automatically install a configuration file to "
"your nginx.  You can find example configuration files for your webserver in "
"the ``contrib/`` directory of your Zammad installation."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/tutorials/webserver-config.md:18
msgid ""
"In case this out-of-the-box approach doesn't work for you, you can find some "
"hints for your configuration. You can use either Nginx or Apache 2 (only "
"referred to as Apache in the following text)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#: src/en/tutorials/webserver-config.md:19
#, no-wrap
msgid "Get a SSL Certificate"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/tutorials/webserver-config.md:25
msgid ""
"You have to use a named configuration which is not configured by default. To "
"fix this, open the ``zammad.conf`` in your webserver's config directory and "
"replace the ``server_name localhost`` (Nginx) or ``ServerName localhost`` "
"(Apache)  with your Zammad domain."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/tutorials/webserver-config.md:27
msgid "The config directories are usually:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/tutorials/webserver-config.md:30
msgid ""
"Nginx: ``/etc/nginx/conf.d/``, ``/etc/nginx/vhosts.d/``, ``/etc/nginx/sites-"
"available/``"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: src/en/tutorials/webserver-config.md:30
msgid ""
"Apache: ``/etc/apache2/conf.d/``, ``/etc/httpd/vhosts.d/``, ``/etc/apache2/"
"sites-available/``"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: src/en/tutorials/webserver-config.md:31
#, no-wrap
msgid "Let's Encrypt"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: src/en/tutorials/webserver-config.md:37
msgid ""
"There are two common tools to get certificates, to which your find a basic "
"configuration below: [certbot](https://certbot.eff.org/instructions) and "
"[acme.sh](https://github.com/acmesh-official/acme.sh/wiki). Have a look at "
"their documentation for further configuration details and other examples."
msgstr ""

#. type: Fenced div block (tabs)
#: src/en/tutorials/webserver-config.md:38
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"\n"
"===certbot\n"
"\n"
"If not happened automatically, you have to install the nginx or apache plugin\n"
"for certbot: ``python3-certbot-nginx`` or ``python3-certbot-apache``\n"
"\n"
"During the first certbot run it will request additional information once.\n"
"Replace ``<webserver>`` in below command by either ``apache``, ``httpd`` or\n"
"``nginx`` to match your setup.\n"
"\n"
"```bash\n"
"certbot --<webserver> -d zammad.example.com\n"
"```\n"
"\n"
"Certbot will now attempt to issue a certificate for you. If successful,\n"
"certbot will ask you if you want to ``[1] not redirect`` or ``[2] redirect``\n"
"automatically. You can choose to not redirect if you plan to use the sample\n"
"configuration of Zammad.\n"
"\n"
"From now on, certbot will automatically renew your installed certificates if\n"
"they’re valid for 30 days or less.\n"
"\n"
"===acme.sh\n"
"\n"
"Change the default certificate authority to Let's encrypt:\n"
"\n"
"```bash\n"
"acme.sh --set-default-ca  --server letsencrypt\n"
"```\n"
"\n"
"Issue your certificate and replace ``<webserver>`` in the following command\n"
"with either ``apache`` or ``nginx`` or ``standalone`` for other webserver.\n"
"\n"
"```bash\n"
"acme.sh --issue --<webserver> -d zammad.example.com\n"
"```\n"
"\n"
"It is not recommended to use the stored certificates directly. You should\n"
"install the certificate to a directory of your choice instead as you can see\n"
"in the next command below. We’re using ``/etc/ssl/private/`` in this case,\n"
"but you can use any directory you like.\n"
"\n"
"Replace ``<webserver>`` with ``apache2``, ``httpd`` or ``nginx``.\n"
"\n"
"```bash\n"
"acme.sh --install-cert -d zammad.example.com \\\n"
"    --cert-file      /etc/ssl/private/zammad.example.com.pem  \\\n"
"    --key-file       /etc/ssl/private/zammad.example.com.key  \\\n"
"    --fullchain-file /etc/ssl/private/zammad.example.com.full.pem \\\n"
"    --reloadcmd     \"systemctl force-reload <webserver>\"\n"
"```\n"
"\n"
"From now on, acme.sh will automatically renew your installed certificates if\n"
"they’re valid for 30 days or less.\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#: src/en/tutorials/webserver-config.md:96
#, no-wrap
msgid "Commercial CA"
msgstr ""

